{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-810", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/810", "wordCount": 3195, "segments": [{"start": 24.0, "text": "I'm sure you're familiar with"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "that sound."}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "It's been part of our life for"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "years. In 2019 though, I think we can"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "do better."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "I'm Camille Moussette,"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "interaction designer on the"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "Apple design team."}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "And, I'm Hugo Verweij, sound"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "designer on the design team."}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "This session is about designing"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "great audio-haptic experiences."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "Our goal, with this talk, is for"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "you to be inspired, and leave"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "you with practical ideas about"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "how to design great sound and"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "haptics when used together in"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "the right way, can bring a new"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "dimension to your app."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "During the next 30 minutes,"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "we'll talk about three things."}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "First we'll introduce what is an"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "audio-haptic experience?"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "Then we'll look at three guiding"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "principles to help you design"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "those great experiences."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "Lastly, we'll look at different"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "techniques, and practical tips,"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "to make those experiences great"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "and truly compelling."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "So, what is an audio-haptic"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "experience?"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "Well, let's start by listening"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "to a sound."}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "OK, now let's lower the sound."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "What happens if I lower it even"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "further?"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "Whoa."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "It's so low I can't hear it any"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "more."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "You know, our ears just don't"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "register it any more."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "But, if you would put your"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "finger on the speaker, you could"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "still feel it move back and"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "forth."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "We designed the Taptic Engine"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "specifically to play these low"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "frequencies that you can only"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "feel."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "Here it is in the iPhone."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "And, next to it, the speaker"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "module."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "The haptic sensations from the"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "Taptic Engine are synchronized"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "to the sounds coming from the"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "speaker."}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "And, the result is what we call"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "an audio-haptic experience."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "But, haptic sensations are meant"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "to be felt, so because we are"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "presenting this on stage, and on"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "screen, we need your help in"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "imaging what this would feel"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "like."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "We'll do our best to help you by"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "visualizing the haptics like"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "Or, by playing a sound that"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "resembles the haptic, like this."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "We will also visualize these"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "experiences on the timeline, and"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "Camille will tell you some more"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "about how that's done in a quick"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "haptics design primer."}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "iOS 13 introduced a new API"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "for designing your own custom"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "haptics."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "It's called Core Haptics."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "This new API allows you"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "developers to use the Taptic"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "Engine fully in iPhone."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "The Taptic Engine is capable of"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "rendering a wide range of"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "It can generate a custom"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "vibration, like this."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "Looks like this, and it should"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "sound and feel like this."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "So, as you've seen, we're using"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "a waveform and sound to"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "represent haptics."}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "As Hugo said, you need to"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "imagine this in your hand as a"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "silent experience."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "This should be felt and not"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "heard. So, we can play these continuous"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "We can also have something"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "that's more shorter and compact."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "It's a single cycle, and we call"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "this experience a transient."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "It's much more momentary, and it"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "feels like an impact, or a"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "strike, or a tap."}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "Very momentary."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "And then we actually can refine"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "it further."}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "Moving forward, we'll use basic"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "shapes to represent haptics in"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "different patterns."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "So, our transient becomes our"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "simple rectangle."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "And, because our Taptic Engine"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "is an exceptional piece of"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "haptic engineering, we can"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "modulate the experience in"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "different ways."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "First, we can modulate the"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "intensity or the amplitude."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "We can also make it feel more"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "round, or soft."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "At the other extreme, we can"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "make it more precise and crisp."}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "So, this experience is possible"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "with the Taptic Engine."}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "So, in the end, this completes"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "our quick introduction to haptic"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "design, and what the Core"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "Haptics API is all about."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "We have one intensity you can"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "modulate, and another design"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "dimension, haptic sharpness,"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "that you are in control for two"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "types of event, continuous and"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "transient."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "Now, let's look at the three"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "guiding principle that we want"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "to share with you today."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "First is causality."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "Then, we have harmony."}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "And, lastly we have utility."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "These concept or approaches are"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "used throughout the work that we"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "do at Apple, and we think they"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "can help you as well in your own"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "app experience."}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "For each of them, we'll look at"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "the concept and explain through"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "a few examples."}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "Let's get started."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "Causality: Causality is about,"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "for feedback to be useful; it"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "must be obvious what caused it."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "So, imagine being a soccer"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "player, kicking this ball."}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "What would the experience feel"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "like?"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "There is a clear relationship,"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "an obvious relationship between"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "the cause-- the foot colliding"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "with the ball-- and the effect--"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "the sound of the impact and the"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "feel of the impact."}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "Now, what this experience sounds"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "and feels like is determined by"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "the qualities of the interacting"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "objects."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "The material of the shoe, the"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "material of the ball, and then,"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "the dynamics of the action."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "Is it a hard kick or a soft"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "kick?"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "And, the environment."}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "The acoustics of the stadium, or"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "the soccer field."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "Because we are so familiar with"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "these things, it would not make"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "sense at all to use a sound that"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "is very different."}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "Let's try it out, and take it"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "way over the top."}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "Very strange. That doesn't really work."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "Now, when designing sounds for"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "your experiences, think about"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "what would it feel and sound"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "like, if what you interact with"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "would be a physical object."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "As an example, let's look at the"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "Apple Pay confirmation."}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "We wanted the sound and the"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "haptics to perfectly match the"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "animation on screen, the check"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "mark."}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "So, where do we start?"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "Well, what sounds do you"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "associate with making a payment?"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "What does money sound like?"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "And, what is the interaction of"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "making a payment, using Apple"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "Pay?"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "And, of course we have to look"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "at that animation of the check"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "mark on screen."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "It should feel positive, like"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "confirming a successful"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "transaction."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "Here are a few examples of"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "sounds that were candidates for"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "this confirmation."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "This the first one."}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "This one is very pleasant."}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "But, it sounded a bit too happy"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "and frivolous."}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "The next one worked really well"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "with the check mark of the"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "animation."}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "But, we felt that its character"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "wasn't really right."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "It was a little too harsh."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "And then, there's this one, the"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "one that we chose in the end."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "And, that you all know."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "It's not too serious, and it's"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "clearly a confirmation."}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "OK. So, we've got our sound."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "Now, on to the haptics."}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "Our first idea was to mimic the"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "waveform of the sound because it"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "matches perfectly, but after"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "some experimentation, we found"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "that two simple taps actually"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "did a better job."}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "I like to see these as little"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "mini-compositions, where we have"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "two instruments; one that you"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "can hear and one that you can"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "feel, the haptics."}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "They don't always necessarily"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "have to play the same thing, but"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "they do have to play in the same"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "tempo."}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "Here they are together."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "Notice the lower sound"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "indicating the haptics."}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "OK. And, this is then the final"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "experience with the animation."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "Again, imagine feeling the taps"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "in your hand when you pay."}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "Next, let's look at our"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "second guiding principle,"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "harmony."}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "Harmony is about things should"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "feel the way they look, the way"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "they sound."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "In the real world, audio,"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "haptics, and visuals are"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "naturally in harmony because of"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "the clear cause and effect"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "relationship."}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "In the digital world, though, we"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "have to do this work manually."}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "New experiences are created in"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "an additive process."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "The input and output need to be"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "specifically designed by you,"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "the developer."}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "Let's start with creating a"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "simple interface with the"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "visual."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "We have a simple sphere dropping"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "and colliding with the bottom of"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "the screen."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Let's add audio feedback."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "Now, we choose a sound that"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "corresponds to a physical"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "impact, or the bounce of the"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "sphere."}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "It needs to be short and precise"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "and clear, but we also modulate"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "the amplitude based on the"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "velocity of the hit."}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "Now, let's do additional work,"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "and introduce the third sense,"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "haptic feedback."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "So, imagine feeling that hit in"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "your hand."}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "Again, we're trying to design in"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "harmony the sphere hitting the"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "bottom of the screen, so we"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "choose a transient event with"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "high sharpness."}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "We also modulate the intensity"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "to match the velocity of the"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "bounce."}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "We're not done yet."}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "Because it's really important to"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "think about synchronization"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "between the three senses."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "That's where the magic happens."}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "That's where the illusion of a"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "real ball colliding with the"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "wall takes shape."}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "So, here's an example where we"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "broke the rules, and we"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "introduced latency between the"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "visual and the rest of the"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "feedback."}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "It's clearly broken, and the"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "illusion of a real bouncing ball"}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "is completely not there."}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "So, harmony requires great care"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "and attention from you, but when"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "done well, can create very"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "delightful and magical"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "Let's look at the different"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "harmony in terms of the notion"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "between interaction, visuals,"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "audio, and haptics."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "In terms of qualities and"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "overall behaviors."}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "We'll look at a simple green dot"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "on screen that we'll animate,"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "and think through what kind of"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "audio, what kind of haptics,"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "make sense with that green dot."}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "So, if we add a snappy pop, or a"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "different pulse, what kind of"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "audio, or what kind of haptics"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "work with these visuals?"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "What if we have a large object"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "on screen?"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "Does it sound different?"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "Does it feel different than a"}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "tiny little dot?"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "If we have different dynamic"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "behavior, different energy"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "level, a pressing, pulsating dot"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "that really calls for attention"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "might want different sound,"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "different haptics."}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "And, lastly, something that"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "feels calm, or like a heartbeat,"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "warrant different type of"}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "feedback."}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "So, think about the pace, the"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "energy level, and the different"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "quality that you're trying to"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "convey in your app."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "Design feedback that tells a"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "consistent and unified story."}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "I'll illustrate how the"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "harmony principle helps us with"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "designing sound and haptics for"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "the Apple Watch crown."}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "We were all used to our phones,"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "and their old-school vibes"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "coming from them, when the Apple"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "Watch came out as the first"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "device with a Taptic Engine."}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "It was the first device that"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "could precisely synchronize"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "sound and haptics."}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "For Series 4, haptics and a very"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "subtle sound were added to the"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "rotation of the crown."}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "Remember the sharp and precise"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "haptic that Camille described"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "earlier?"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "That was the one that we used"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "for the crown."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "But, it was scaled down to match"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "the small size of the crown."}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "And so, the haptics are felt in"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "the finger touching the crown,"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "rather than on the wrist."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "For sounds, we looked at the"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "world of traditional watch"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "making for inspiration."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "We listened to and recorded all"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "kinds of different watches, some"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "of which sounded quite remarkable, like this one."}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "And then, there are other"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "physical-- mechanical objects in"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "the real world, with a similar"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "sound, like bicycle hubs."}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "We wanted to find a sound that"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "would feel natural coming from a"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "device like this."}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "We took these sounds as"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "inspiration before we started"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "crafting our own."}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "And, this is the result."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "On your wrist, it sounds very"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "quiet, just like you would"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "expect coming from a watch."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "The perfect coordination between"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "sound and haptics creates the"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "illusion of a mechanical crown."}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "And then, to match this"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "mechanical sensation, our motion"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "team changed the animation so it"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "snaps to the sound and the"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "haptics when using the crown."}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "Let's look at that."}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "And, I'll play it again."}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "Look at the crown, visualizing"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "the haptics."}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "The result is a precise"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "mechanical feel, which is in"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "perfect harmony with what you"}, {"start": 934.0, "text": "see and what you hear."}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "Next, let's look at our third"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "guiding principle, utility."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "Utility is about adding audio"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "and haptic feedback only when"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "you can provide clear value and"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "benefit to your app experience."}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "Use moderation."}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "Don't add sound and haptics just"}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "because you can."}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "Let's look at a simple ARKit app"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "that we made to illustrate this"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "point."}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "In this app, we place a virtual"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "timer in the environment, and"}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "the interaction is dependent on"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "the distance to that virtual"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "timer."}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "Let's look at the video first."}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "So, in this app, we purposely"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "designed audio-haptic feedback"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "to complement the AR interaction"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "and the most significant part of"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "the user experience."}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "Meaning moving closer to the"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "timer, or moving away from the"}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "timer, modulate the audio-haptic"}, {"start": 1006.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "The three senses are coherent"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "and unified."}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "We refrain from adding other"}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "sound effects, or haptic"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "feedback, to interacting with"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "the different elements, or other"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "minor interaction in the app."}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "It is often a good idea not"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "to add sound in haptics."}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "So, start by identifying"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "possible locations in your app"}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "for audio-haptic feedback, and"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "then focus only on the elements"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "where it can enhance the experience, or communicate"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "something important."}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "And then, are you tempted to add"}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "more?"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "Well, maybe don't."}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "It will overwhelm people, and it"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "will diminish the value of"}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "what's really important."}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "So, to recap, here are the"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "guiding principles one more"}, {"start": 1053.0, "text": "time."}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "We spoke about causality."}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "How it can help to think about"}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "what makes the sound, and what"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "causes the haptics."}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "About harmony."}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "How sound, haptics, and visuals"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "work together in creating a"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "great experience."}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "And, utility."}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "How looking at the experience"}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "from the point of view of the"}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "human using your app."}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "Next, let's look at the"}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "techniques that-- and, practical"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "tips, that we can use with these"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "three guiding principle to"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "create great audio-haptic"}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "First, a small recap about the"}, {"start": 1095.0, "text": "primitive available in Core"}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "Haptics."}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "We have two building blocks that"}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "you can work with."}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "The first one is called"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "transient, and is a sharp,"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "compact haptic experience that"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "you can feel, like a tap or a"}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "strike."}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "The second one is a continuous"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "haptic experience that extend"}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "over time. You can specify the duration."}, {"start": 1117.0, "text": "How long it should last."}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "For transient, there are two"}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "design dimensions that is"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "available and under your"}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "control."}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "We have haptic intensity, and we"}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "have haptic sharpness, to create"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "something more round or soft at"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "the lower value."}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "And, something more precise,"}, {"start": 1135.0, "text": "mechanical, and crisp at the"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "upper bound."}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "Intensity changes the amplitude"}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "of the experience as expected."}, {"start": 1144.0, "text": "For continuous, we have the two"}, {"start": 1147.0, "text": "similar design dimensions."}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "We have sharpness and intensity,"}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "and we're able to create more"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "organic, or rumble-like"}, {"start": 1156.0, "text": "experience that extends over"}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "time, or something that is more"}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "precise, and more mechanical at"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "the upper values of sharpness."}, {"start": 1162.0, "text": "But, there are more many more"}, {"start": 1164.0, "text": "details and capabilities in the"}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "Core Haptics API."}, {"start": 1167.0, "text": "Be sure to check out the online"}, {"start": 1169.0, "text": "documentation."}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "Now, when designing sounds,"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "keep in mind what will work best"}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "with these haptics."}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "For a sharp transient, a chime"}, {"start": 1180.0, "text": "with a sharp attack will"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "probably work really well."}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "But, if we have a sound that's"}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "much smoother, using those same"}, {"start": 1188.0, "text": "haptics is probably not such a"}, {"start": 1190.0, "text": "good idea."}, {"start": 1194.0, "text": "So, for something like this, a"}, {"start": 1197.0, "text": "continuous haptic, ramping up"}, {"start": 1198.0, "text": "and down probably works better."}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "But, these are not hard rules."}, {"start": 1206.0, "text": "There's a lot of room to"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "experiment."}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "And, sometimes, you may find out"}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "that the opposite of what you"}, {"start": 1213.0, "text": "thought would work is actually"}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "better. And, this was the case for the"}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "Apple Watch alarm that sounds"}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "like this."}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "For a sound like this, you may"}, {"start": 1225.0, "text": "want to add a haptic like this,"}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "because it pairs together"}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "perfectly."}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "But, can we make it better?"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "Can we keep experimenting?"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "Maybe flip it around and change"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "the timing?"}, {"start": 1245.0, "text": "This creates anticipation by"}, {"start": 1247.0, "text": "ramping up the haptics and then"}, {"start": 1249.0, "text": "quickly cutting it off and"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "playing the sound."}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "There's a clear action-reaction,"}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "and the sound plays as an answer"}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "to the haptic."}, {"start": 1257.0, "text": "This works really well for the"}, {"start": 1258.0, "text": "Apple Watch alarm."}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "Next, it's pretty common to"}, {"start": 1265.0, "text": "have a number of events"}, {"start": 1266.0, "text": "back-to-back to convey different"}, {"start": 1268.0, "text": "type of experience."}, {"start": 1270.0, "text": "In this case, we have four"}, {"start": 1272.0, "text": "transient event."}, {"start": 1274.0, "text": "And, we notice that when we"}, {"start": 1275.0, "text": "present this to different"}, {"start": 1276.0, "text": "people, they don't necessarily"}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "feel the first one."}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "We have the first ghost haptics."}, {"start": 1284.0, "text": "So, the sequence of four taps is"}, {"start": 1285.0, "text": "actually reported as a triple"}, {"start": 1287.0, "text": "tap only."}, {"start": 1289.0, "text": "This could be a problem, or an"}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "opportunity."}, {"start": 1294.0, "text": "We could use this effect of"}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "ghost, or not perceiving the"}, {"start": 1297.0, "text": "first one completely, as a"}, {"start": 1298.0, "text": "priming effect."}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "Let's look at the example of a"}, {"start": 1303.0, "text": "third-party alert on watchOS."}, {"start": 1305.0, "text": "This is the sound and the"}, {"start": 1306.0, "text": "haptics of that third-party"}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "notification."}, {"start": 1312.0, "text": "So, this is a really important"}, {"start": 1313.0, "text": "notification that we want to"}, {"start": 1315.0, "text": "make sure the user perceive and"}, {"start": 1317.0, "text": "acknowledge clearly."}, {"start": 1319.0, "text": "So, in this case, we use our"}, {"start": 1322.0, "text": "ghost effect, or our primer in"}, {"start": 1324.0, "text": "this case, to wake up the skin,"}, {"start": 1327.0, "text": "and make sure that it's"}, {"start": 1328.0, "text": "completely ready to feel what's"}, {"start": 1330.0, "text": "to come."}, {"start": 1332.0, "text": "Let's listen and feel it."}, {"start": 1339.0, "text": "So, in this case, we have a"}, {"start": 1341.0, "text": "clear presentation and"}, {"start": 1342.0, "text": "recognition of our main"}, {"start": 1344.0, "text": "notification experience."}, {"start": 1346.0, "text": "Next, we can also create"}, {"start": 1348.0, "text": "contrast between very similar"}, {"start": 1351.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "Here is the sound for the left"}, {"start": 1355.0, "text": "navigation cue on watchOS."}, {"start": 1358.0, "text": "It sounds like this."}, {"start": 1364.0, "text": "With our harmony guiding"}, {"start": 1366.0, "text": "principle, we end up with really"}, {"start": 1369.0, "text": "nice haptic that pairs really"}, {"start": 1371.0, "text": "well with that sound."}, {"start": 1372.0, "text": "So, we have a series of double"}, {"start": 1373.0, "text": "strike, that sound and feels"}, {"start": 1375.0, "text": "like this."}, {"start": 1381.0, "text": "Now, if we look at the right"}, {"start": 1383.0, "text": "cue, we have a similar sound,"}, {"start": 1386.0, "text": "but slightly different."}, {"start": 1391.0, "text": "So we can notice the little"}, {"start": 1393.0, "text": "difference between the left and"}, {"start": 1394.0, "text": "the right on the audio, but if"}, {"start": 1396.0, "text": "we continue to follow our"}, {"start": 1398.0, "text": "harmony principle, with the"}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "haptics we end up with the"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "identical pattern between the"}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "left and the right experience."}, {"start": 1406.0, "text": "In this case, we want to add"}, {"start": 1409.0, "text": "haptics-- we double up haptics"}, {"start": 1412.0, "text": "from the double strikes."}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "And then, we have true contrast"}, {"start": 1415.0, "text": "between left and right."}, {"start": 1417.0, "text": "Let's listen and feel what--"}, {"start": 1421.0, "text": "this experience."}, {"start": 1426.0, "text": "Again, we have contrast between"}, {"start": 1428.0, "text": "the left and the right for very"}, {"start": 1429.0, "text": "similar audio experience."}, {"start": 1433.0, "text": "So, by now, you have quite a"}, {"start": 1435.0, "text": "few tools to create your own"}, {"start": 1437.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 1439.0, "text": "We would like to show you one"}, {"start": 1440.0, "text": "more example to illustrate the"}, {"start": 1442.0, "text": "points we made."}, {"start": 1443.0, "text": "This is a full-screen effect in"}, {"start": 1445.0, "text": "Messages."}, {"start": 1451.0, "text": "The sound and haptics are"}, {"start": 1452.0, "text": "perfectly synchronized to the"}, {"start": 1453.0, "text": "animation."}, {"start": 1454.0, "text": "And, it's a delightful moment"}, {"start": 1455.0, "text": "for a special occasion."}, {"start": 1457.0, "text": "Let's look at it one more time."}, {"start": 1465.0, "text": "Now, if you haven't yet, I"}, {"start": 1466.0, "text": "encourage you to try this out on"}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": "your own iPhone, to experience"}, {"start": 1471.0, "text": "the haptics yourself."}, {"start": 1474.0, "text": "And now, a few more thoughts to"}, {"start": 1475.0, "text": "consider in addition to the"}, {"start": 1477.0, "text": "guiding principles that we"}, {"start": 1478.0, "text": "shared."}, {"start": 1481.0, "text": "The best results come when"}, {"start": 1482.0, "text": "sound, haptics, and visuals are"}, {"start": 1485.0, "text": "designed hand-in-hand."}, {"start": 1487.0, "text": "Are you an animator?"}, {"start": 1489.0, "text": "Collaborate with a sound or"}, {"start": 1490.0, "text": "interaction designer and vice"}, {"start": 1492.0, "text": "versa."}, {"start": 1493.0, "text": "It's the best way to come to a"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "unified experience."}, {"start": 1497.0, "text": "Imagine using your own app for"}, {"start": 1500.0, "text": "the very first time."}, {"start": 1502.0, "text": "What would you like it to sound"}, {"start": 1504.0, "text": "like, or feel like?"}, {"start": 1506.0, "text": "And, then imagine using it 100"}, {"start": 1508.0, "text": "times more."}, {"start": 1510.0, "text": "Does it still help you to hear"}, {"start": 1512.0, "text": "and feel these things?"}, {"start": 1514.0, "text": "Or, are you overwhelmed?"}, {"start": 1516.0, "text": "Experience it, and take away all"}, {"start": 1519.0, "text": "the things that don't feel"}, {"start": 1520.0, "text": "compelling, or that are not"}, {"start": 1521.0, "text": "useful."}, {"start": 1522.0, "text": "And, don't be afraid to"}, {"start": 1525.0, "text": "experiment."}, {"start": 1526.0, "text": "Try things out."}, {"start": 1527.0, "text": "Prototype."}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "We've seen that you may just"}, {"start": 1530.0, "text": "come across something amazing,"}, {"start": 1531.0, "text": "by trying something new."}, {"start": 1534.0, "text": "We're looking forward to seeing,"}, {"start": 1536.0, "text": "hearing, and feeling what you"}, {"start": 1538.0, "text": "will come up with in your own"}, {"start": 1540.0, "text": "apps."}, {"start": 1541.0, "text": "See this URL for more"}, {"start": 1542.0, "text": "information."}]}
